PROJECT STRUCTURE AND ARCHITECTURE MAP
======================================

Project: Transient_Diffusion2D_FDM_Solvers_Cpp
Domain: Two-dimensional transient diffusion solved with finite-difference methods.
Language: C++20.
Build system: CMake 3.20 or newer.
Primary include convention: project-root-relative paths, for example
  #include "Core/Field/Field.hpp"

PURPOSE AND READING GUIDE
-------------------------
This file describes the current source layout, module responsibilities, numerical
conventions, simulation data flow, and CMake targets. It is intended as a compact
architecture guide for developers and AI coding assistants.

- .hpp files declare interfaces, data structures, inline utilities, and templates.
- .cpp files contain out-of-line implementations and are listed in CMake targets.
- [entry point] marks a translation unit containing main().
- Results/, bin/, and build/ contain runtime or generated artifacts and are summarized.
- The repository root is added as an include directory to project libraries/executables.
- README files are not required to interpret this map.

